    },
    {
      "name": "Session",
      "description": "Getting a token. THE API ISSUES THEM NOW \u2014 it is its own authorization server (ADR 18), where it previously only verified tokens minted by Auth0.\n\n\u26a1 THE LOCAL SHORTCUT, and what you probably want:\n\n    npm run db:seed:dev\n    npm run --silent auth:token --workspace=api -- admin\n\nThat mints a real access token for a seeded user and prints it; paste it into {{token}}. `admin`, `contributor` and `user` pick which seeded row it names. It signs with the same key the API verifies with, so it is not a test double \u2014 the only thing making it safe is that JWT_SIGNING_KEYS is per environment.\n\nAgainst staging you cannot do that, so you need a real sign-in: use the browser at {{webBaseUrl}} and take the id_token, then run Start session.\n\nA token does not carry your rank. It carries only `sub` \u2014 which is User.id, this API's own identifier, not Google's \u2014 and role is read from that row on every request. Changing a role in the database applies to the next request, with no new token and no re-login.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Start session (Google ID token) \u2192 saves {{token}} + {{refreshToken}}",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idToken\": \"{{googleIdToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/session",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "session"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges a Google ID token for this API's own token pair, creating the account if the subject has never been seen.\n\nGETTING AN ID TOKEN IS THE AWKWARD PART, and there is no way around it in Postman: it is issued by Google to a caller holding the client secret, which only the web app has. Sign in at {{webBaseUrl}} and take the id_token from the callback, or skip this request entirely \u2014 see the folder description for the local shortcut.\n\n@Public, because the caller has no token from this API yet. That is what this endpoint is for. It is not unauthenticated: the handler verifies Google's signature, issuer, audience and email_verified before anything else happens.\n\nIdempotent per sign-in \u2014 calling it again re-syncs the profile, moves lastLoginAt, and opens a NEW session, which is correct because each sign-in is one."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "",
                  "const tokens = body && body.data && body.data.tokens;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 with a token pair', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(tokens && tokens.accessToken, 'no accessToken').to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(tokens && tokens.refreshToken, 'no refreshToken').to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (tokens) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('token', tokens.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('refreshToken', tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('Saved {{token}} and {{refreshToken}}. Access token expires in ' +",
                  "        tokens.expiresIn + 's.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    // Leave the old values alone rather than blanking them: a transient",
                  "    // failure should not also log you out of every other request.",
                  "    console.log('Nothing saved; the previous {{token}} is unchanged.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh \u2192 rotates, saves the new pair",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Spends {{refreshToken}} and returns a new pair.\n\nSINGLE USE. The token you send is dead the moment this returns, which is why the test script overwrites both variables. Sending the same one twice is treated as theft and revokes the whole session \u2014 try it and watch the next request fail.\n\nThe absolute deadline (30 days) belongs to the login and does NOT reset here; only the 14-day idle deadline does. A session refreshed forever still ends."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "",
                  "const tokens = body && body.data && body.data.tokens;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 with a token pair', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(tokens && tokens.accessToken, 'no accessToken').to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(tokens && tokens.refreshToken, 'no refreshToken').to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (tokens) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('token', tokens.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('refreshToken', tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('Saved {{token}} and {{refreshToken}}. Access token expires in ' +",
                  "        tokens.expiresIn + 's.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    // Leave the old values alone rather than blanking them: a transient",
                  "    // failure should not also log you out of every other request.",
                  "    console.log('Nothing saved; the previous {{token}} is unchanged.');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
                  "    console.log('Session over. Either the token was already spent \u2014 which revokes the whole family \u2014 or it expired. Start a new session.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log out \u2192 ends this session",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes every token in this session's family.\n\nTakes the refresh token rather than the access token, because an access token names a USER and this has to name a SESSION \u2014 signing out here must not sign you out on another device.\n\nSucceeds for a token that does not exist, deliberately: logging out is not a place to tell a caller whether a credential was real, and what they asked for is true either way."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// The pair is dead server-side; clearing it locally keeps the",
                  "// environment honest about that.",
                  "pm.environment.set('token', '');",
                  "pm.environment.set('refreshToken', '');",
                  "console.log('Cleared {{token}} and {{refreshToken}}.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dictionary \u2014 reads (public)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Browse entries",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "type",
                  "value": "WORD",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "WORD | EXPRESSION (PHRASE is rejected \u2014 lesson-only)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "partOfSpeech",
                  "value": "NOUN",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "NOUN|VERB|ADJECTIVE|ADVERB|PRONOUN|PARTICLE|PREPOSITION|CONJUNCTION|OTHER"
                },
                {
                  "key": "dialectCode",
                  "value": "common",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "isPublished",
                  "value": "true",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "CONTRIBUTOR+ only; ignored for public requests"
                },
                {
                  "key": "locale",
                  "value": "en",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "es (default) | en \u2014 resolves gloss/example language"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Paginated browse. Public. Returns WORD/EXPRESSION only."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Search entries",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/search?q=takat",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "search"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "takat",
                  "description": "required; pg_trgm fuzzy match"
                },
                {
                  "key": "type",
                  "value": "WORD",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "dialectCode",
                  "value": "common",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fuzzy search. `q` is required (400 without it). Public."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Entry by slug",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/entries/by-slug/{{slug}}?locale=es",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["entries", "by-slug", "{{slug}}"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "locale",
                  "value": "es",
                  "disabled": true
